  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Thai Nguyen VCA-509216</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Thai Nguyen tea value chain becomes more sustainable, climate resilience, and gender responsive contributing to local social and economic development.
The project will prioritize supporting tea producers and processors in disadvantaged areas that have not yet accessed/optimized available supports, especially cooperatives and groups with the participation of women, ethnic minority and small-scaled households. Some cooperatives with a higher level of readiness in terms of production capacity and operational management will be supported to pilot organic tea and low-emission tea production practices as models for future replication.
The tentative project sites are 03 communes in Dai Tu, Dinh Hoa, and Dong Hy districts, where: farming practices are still conventional resulting in low-value tea products; women and ethnic minority are the main labor force in tea production with limited accessed to technical supports and financial resources. The total number of tea producers expected to directly benefit from the project&#x2019;s intervention in the target sites is 500 farmers, among which, ~60% are women and ~10% are ethnic minority.</narrative>
  </description>
